From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:27:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] packaging: build SHA-derived peer-compatible package

Record the exact upstream base and document the maintained patch stack. Add a manually dispatched workflow that verifies one exact source commit, appends source-derived SemVer build metadata, embeds full source and upstream provenance, and uploads the packed artifact.

Keep the source package name and version unchanged in Git. Build metadata identifies the fork without turning it into a prerelease, so packages declaring an ordinary convex@^1.x peer remain compatible. The immutable full-SHA artifact URL remains the installation and provenance boundary.
